 "publicacion": {
  "titulo": "America now pays more in interest than on defense",
  "descripcion": "US federal interest payments ran at a $1.33 trillion annual rate in Q3 2026, against $1.23 trillion for national defense: $1.08 for every defense dollar, up from 62 cents in early 2020. Interest passed defense in Q1 2024 and has stayed above since (it also did for one quarter, Q1 1998). The money goes to bondholders, and interest does not reduce the debt. Gross interest; defense = consumption + gross investment. Ratios are our own calculation from BEA data via FRED. Not financial advice. The appearance of U.S. Department of War (DoW) visual information does not imply or constitute DoW endorsement. #shorts #economy #nationaldebt #money"
 },
